From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] egl: keep the libEGL whose eglGetProcAddress is kept

get_egl_proc_address() finds eglGetProcAddress in the libEGL the program
loaded and keeps the pointer for good, without holding that library.
SDL2 closes libEGL when it recreates its renderer (ScummVM at start):
the next call jumped into unmapped memory, an instruction abort as
ScummVM started with the FPS overlay on (R36S, panfrost). Keep
that libEGL loaded (RTLD_NODELETE) once its pointer is kept.

---
--- a/src/gl/inject_egl.cpp	2026-11-26 22:51:07.849700832 -0300
+++ b/src/gl/inject_egl.cpp	2026-11-26 22:51:07.863524980 -0300
@@ -57,6 +57,12 @@
             if (ret) continue;
 
             eh_find_sym(&lib_egl, "eglGetProcAddress", (void **)&pfn_eglGetProcAddress);
+            /* The pointer is kept for good, but the program loaded libEGL
+             * and may unload it (SDL2 closes it when it recreates its
+             * renderer: ScummVM): the next call then jumps into unmapped
+             * memory. Keep that libEGL loaded from now on. */
+            if (pfn_eglGetProcAddress && lib_egl.name && *lib_egl.name)
+                dlopen(lib_egl.name, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_NOLOAD | RTLD_NODELETE);
             eh_destroy_obj(&lib_egl);
 
             if (pfn_eglGetProcAddress) break;
